WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.839
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:09.362
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:15.832
Unit seven: Clothes & Style. Today you will describe clothes using adjectives in the right order.

4
00:00:16.132 --> 00:00:18.889
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.833 --> 00:00:23.217
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:24.083 --> 00:00:24.933
Trendy.

7
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:28.286
Trendy means very fashionable right now.

8
00:00:28.883 --> 00:00:30.581
She wears trendy jeans.

9
00:00:31.183 --> 00:00:33.453
Your turn. Say: Trendy.

10
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.011
Trendy.

11
00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:38.739
Outfit.

12
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.005
Outfit means a set of clothes worn together.

13
00:00:42.617 --> 00:00:43.989
I love your outfit!

14
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:47.236
Your turn. Say: Outfit.

15
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.031
Outfit.

16
00:00:51.783 --> 00:00:52.680
Casual.

17
00:00:53.683 --> 00:00:55.927
Casual means relaxed, not formal.

18
00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:58.632
I wear casual clothes on weekends.

19
00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:01.544
Your turn. Say: Casual.

20
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.343
Casual.

21
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:06.887
Formal.

22
00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:10.754
Formal means for serious or special events.

23
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.524
We wear formal clothes to weddings.

24
00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:16.084
Your turn. Say: Formal.

25
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:19.772
Formal.

26
00:01:20.517 --> 00:01:21.599
Accessory.

27
00:01:22.583 --> 00:01:26.429
Accessory means a small extra item like a watch or a bag.

28
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:29.086
A watch is a useful accessory.

29
00:01:29.683 --> 00:01:32.568
Your turn. Say: Accessory.

30
00:01:35.433 --> 00:01:36.551
Accessory.

31
00:01:37.317 --> 00:01:38.190
Fabric.

32
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:41.787
Fabric means material for making clothes.

33
00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:44.267
Cotton is a soft fabric.

34
00:01:44.883 --> 00:01:47.269
Your turn. Say: Fabric.

35
00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:50.925
Fabric.

36
00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:52.336
Fit.

37
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.245
Fit means to be the right size.

38
00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.501
These shoes fit perfectly.

39
00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.374
Your turn. Say: Fit.

40
00:02:03.233 --> 00:02:03.991
Fit.

41
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:05.658
Comfortable.

42
00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:09.126
Comfortable means nice to wear, not tight.

43
00:02:09.717 --> 00:02:11.298
Sneakers are comfortable.

44
00:02:11.883 --> 00:02:14.559
Your turn. Say: Comfortable.

45
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.273
Comfortable.

46
00:02:19.017 --> 00:02:20.134
Fashionable.

47
00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.707
Fashionable means popular and in style.

48
00:02:24.317 --> 00:02:26.572
That jacket is very fashionable.

49
00:02:27.183 --> 00:02:29.696
Your turn. Say: Fashionable.

50
00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:33.767
Fashionable.

51
00:02:34.517 --> 00:02:35.576
Sneakers.

52
00:02:36.583 --> 00:02:39.094
Sneakers means soft sports shoes.

53
00:02:39.683 --> 00:02:41.660
I wear white sneakers to school.

54
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.635
Your turn. Say: Sneakers.

55
00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:48.629
Sneakers.

56
00:02:49.383 --> 00:02:50.175
Hoodie.

57
00:02:51.183 --> 00:02:53.334
Hoodie means a soft top with a hood.

58
00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:55.508
I wear a hoodie when it's cold.

59
00:02:56.117 --> 00:02:58.676
Your turn. Say: Hoodie.

60
00:03:01.533 --> 00:03:02.233
Hoodie.

61
00:03:02.983 --> 00:03:03.950
Style.

62
00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.205
Style means a person's way of dressing.

63
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:10.014
Her style is simple and smart.

64
00:03:10.617 --> 00:03:13.559
Your turn. Say: Style.

65
00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.517
Style.

66
00:03:18.333 --> 00:03:22.356
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:23.217 --> 00:03:25.704
Visal, how would you describe your style?

68
00:03:26.817 --> 00:03:31.756
I like a casual style. I wear comfortable sneakers every day.

69
00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.931
What's your favorite piece of clothing?

70
00:03:36.017 --> 00:03:38.214
My comfortable blue cotton hoodie.

71
00:03:39.317 --> 00:03:41.096
Do you ever wear formal clothes?

72
00:03:42.183 --> 00:03:45.695
Only at weddings. I wear a smart black jacket.

73
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:48.717
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:49.583 --> 00:03:51.885
Grammar focus: Adjective order.

75
00:03:52.185 --> 00:03:53.488
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:54.183 --> 00:03:55.835
a comfortable blue hoodie

77
00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.424
a trendy black jacket

78
00:03:59.317 --> 00:04:01.189
a beautiful new silk dress

79
00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:06.954
Opinion comes first, then size or age, then color, then material.

80
00:04:07.717 --> 00:04:10.764
Be careful! Don't say: a blue comfortable hoodie

81
00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:14.943
Say: a comfortable blue hoodie

82
00:04:15.243 --> 00:04:17.069
Opinion comes before color.

83
00:04:17.867 --> 00:04:20.728
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:21.533 --> 00:04:22.651
What We Wear.

85
00:04:22.951 --> 00:04:26.366
I like a casual style with comfortable sneakers and a hoodie.

86
00:04:27.367 --> 00:04:30.388
My sister prefers trendy, fashionable outfits.

87
00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.352
Today she is wearing a beautiful long silk skirt.

88
00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:39.201
For school, we both wear a white shirt and navy trousers or a skirt.

89
00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.490
Clothes are a fun way to show your style.

90
00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.370
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:48.217 --> 00:04:49.821
Which order is correct?

92
00:04:50.121 --> 00:04:56.016
A, a nice red cotton shirt. B, a red nice cotton shirt. C, a cotton red nice shirt.

93
00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:02.298
The answer is A: a nice red cotton shirt.

94
00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:05.717
A set of clothes worn together is an blank.

95
00:05:06.017 --> 00:05:09.925
A, outfit. B, accessory. C, fabric.

96
00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:15.420
The answer is A: outfit.

97
00:05:16.583 --> 00:05:18.711
Relaxed, not formal, is blank.

98
00:05:19.011 --> 00:05:22.478
A, casual. B, trendy. C, formal.

99
00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:27.940
The answer is A: casual.

100
00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:32.192
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:35.177
Describe your typical outfit for school.

102
00:05:43.983 --> 00:05:45.402
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:45.702 --> 00:05:55.541
I usually wear a clean white shirt, long navy trousers and comfortable black sneakers. My style is simple and casual.

104
00:05:55.841 --> 00:05:57.446
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:02.361
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and adjective order.

106
00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:07.542
Today's value is self-acceptance. Big or little, you are special.

107
00:06:07.842 --> 00:06:10.216
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

108
00:06:10.516 --> 00:06:14.143
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

